Nick Vargish <nav+posts@bandersnatch.org> writes:

> I'm not sure if the Unix/OS-X pre-compiled binaries expect data files
> to be in /usr/games or if they are more flexible than they used to

They expect /usr/games/lib/nethackdir.
But when you compile the game yourself, you can put the variable files
elsewhere by #defining VAR_PLAYGROUND in include/unixconf.h and changing
the VARDIR definition in the top Makefile.
(The OP mentioned compiling a patched version anyway, so this shouldn't be
 a problem.)

